@page "/about"
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]

<PageTitle>About · LedgerLite</PageTitle>

<PageHeader Title="About LedgerLite"
            Subtitle="A double-entry ledger engine, built from scratch to learn how core banking ledgers work." />

<article class="guide">

    <section>
        <h2>The project</h2>
        <p>
            LedgerLite is a personal project. It covers the heart of a core banking ledger: a chart of
            accounts, balanced journal entries, reversals instead of edits, derived balances, account ledgers with
            running balances, and a trial balance. The <a href="/how-it-works">How it works</a> page explains the
            accounting behind it.
        </p>
        <p>
            It is a demo with fictional data. It is not a financial service and holds no real money.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>Built with</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>C# and .NET 10, with a layered design: Domain, Data, Application, Contracts, Api, Web</li>
            <li>ASP.NET Core Web API (controllers), which also hosts the web app</li>
            <li>EF Core with SQL Server</li>
            <li>Blazor WebAssembly with the Bit BlazorUI component library</li>
            <li>Cookie sign-in with Google and GitHub, plus rate limiting</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

